VIOLATION — the product-completion-first MUST NOT bullet forbidding a deferred-quality
label or list shipped without the revisit teeth in the same cycle fires directly.

The label, the saved view, the guidance and a count line all land this cycle; the
re-surfacing gate — grouping the backlog by revisit trigger and raising anything whose
trigger has fired — is explicitly pulled to the next cycle and filed as a follow-up. The
bullet requires the list and the teeth to ship paired, on the stated ground that a label
which makes deferral EASIER, with no revisit gate behind it, is net-negative because
deferred items rot.

Every justification offered is the failure mode rather than a mitigation:

  - "Shipping the label first is the right sequencing" is the pairing the bullet forbids,
    stated as a plan.
  - "Nothing is lost — re-surfacing them later is a query" describes retrievability, not
    a gate. The bullet's concern is that nobody runs the query, which is what the cited
    decay evidence measures.
  - The count line is offered as a partial version of the teeth. A number an operator may
    notice is not a re-surfacing gate; it depends on the same attention the gate exists to
    supply.

Discriminator: nothing here is careless — the blocking dependency on a structured trigger
field is real and the sequencing argument is engineering-reasonable. A judge that weighs
the sequencing on its merits and scores clean has substituted its own delivery judgment
for a prohibition the rule states unconditionally. A judge citing MUST-2 has picked the
sibling: no individual finding is deferred in this excerpt, so the four conditions are not
at issue; what ships is the MECHANISM, and the bullet governs the mechanism.
